    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d732">

                <pb facs="1214" n="1200" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1200"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115/62860: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-08-09T09:00:00+01:00">August 9, 1944—9
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5150. American Interests—Allied Liberated Italy. Department’s 2388, July
                        12.<anchor n="28" xml:id="d732-f1"/> Swiss report that Swiss Legation Rome
                    transmitted through Swiss Consulate Algiers message indicating it continues
                    protect American interests Allied liberated areas of Italy on basis of
                    instructions given by Swiss Foreign Office at request Allied authorities. Swiss
                    Legation Home continues pay relief qualified Americans.</p>
                <p>Swiss Foreign Office official states orally courier Bern-Algiers again
                    functioning and anticipates that documentation and relief applications submitted
                    by Americans in subject areas will be forwarded Bern via that mail channel.
                    Accordingly Swiss willing employ same channel in forwarding Legation’s relief
                    and documentation decisions.</p>
                <p>In view foregoing please instruct whether ultimate sentence Department’s telegram
                    under reference may be considered canceled.<anchor n="29" xml:id="d732-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d732-f1" n="28" xml:id="d732-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d732-f2" n="29" xml:id="d732-f2-content">
                <p>The ultimate sentence was: “Further documentation decisions involving persons in
                    liberated areas of Italy should be referred to Department.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
